{EMBED HERE}
3.1934.307Avery discloses an aircraft 1 with an antitorque tunnel 19 that extends diagonally through the aircraft 1 at the rear end of the fuselage 6, and an auxiliary airscrew or propeller 21 in the tunnel 19. In Avery, the tunnel 19 is normally closed tightly by adjustable louvers 20. As shown in Figures 1-3 of Avery, the louvers extend entirely across the tunnel 19, with each end connected to the shroud for the tunnel, and the louvers do not connect to a gearbox fairing. Furthermore, Applicant submits that Avery does not disclose a gearbox fairing. Avery teaches that the "the louver control rods 36 and the propeller pitch control 26 are so interrelated in their action that the louvers 20 remain closed as long as propeller 21 is at zero pitch, but automatically open in synchronism with the increase of propeller pitch until they stand substantially parallel to tunnel 19." (Column 4, Lines 47-65).
